      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The beta-dependent circular-ensemble generators and their limiting special-function factors together separate a shared Gaussian mechanism from symmetry-class memory: for COE, CUE, and CSE, logarithmically divergent variance with convergent higher cumulants yields normalized Gaussian real and phase logs, but beta-dependent variance constants and the gamma/Barnes-G prefactors' poles, zeros, and integer special values remain different for the ensembles after the common endpoint is factored out.",
